            <ArticleTitle>Chronic heel pain. Treatment rationale.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>563-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic heel pain needs a treatment rationale. Most heel pain responds to conservative treatment. When surgery is done, the surgeon must be aware of the anatomy and especially the nerves about the heel that can cause pain. The author's experience is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
